ine/godot/pull/111528#issuecomment-3576788770","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111528","id":3576788770,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VMXci","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T17:38:44Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T17:38:44Z","body":"Yesterday, to match the upgrade and downgrade chevrons, I made a sideways \"convert\" chevron icon to indicate that the current project version is unknown but opening the project would convert it to the current version (so unknown if it's an upgrade or downgrade).\r\n\r\nAs for using a question mark icon, it appears the version label itself already displays a question mark. As such, I think another one for the conversion icon would be redundant, in addition to not matching the other icons conveying how the project will change if opened, rather than just the current state of the project.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1136\" height=\"300\" alt=\"CleanShot 2025-11-25 at 09 35 50@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5610b0f-f859-4119-ad62-6894f7384485\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"http